[I] Libraries to write tests in C, C++ and shell

[T] ATF (Automated Testing Framework) is a collection of libraries to write
[T] test programs in C, C++ and POSIX shell, with an orthogonal API across
[T] the bindings. ATF-based test programs offer a consistent command-line
[T] interface and are run by an execution engine such as Kyua.

[U] https://github.com/freebsd/atf

[A] Atf Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[F] CROSS
[C] extra/base

[V] 0.26.1
[L] BSD BSD

[D] bfd0ec87ad926df1062fa6dc39ba7f1257644744fa4269a7a8842ab3 atf-0.26.1.tar.gz https://github.com/freebsd/atf/archive/refs/tags/atf-0.26.1/

autogen=2

atstage cross && export kyua_cv_getopt_plus=yes kyua_cv_attribute_noreturn=yes kyua_cv_getcwd_works=yes
